  "declared_lateral_floor_withdrawn": {
    "floor_m": 0.001,
    "why": "The candidate file declared a 1 mm floor on the installed clearance between the cable's clip crossing and the retention predicate's own lateral wall. The screen measures that this floor rejects L1, the validated v2/v3 layout the whole repository is built on: its three cells install at 0.14, 1.87 and 1.05 mm of clearance. A criterion that rejects the reference cannot be the right criterion, so it is withdrawn rather than tuned, and the clearance is reported for every cell as a diagnostic instead. It is the same measurement evidence/cable_discretisation_v4.json reports: this task installs its cable close to the label's boundary, which is a property of the task worth stating rather than a property of these candidates.",
    "kept": "The declared verdict above is kept in full so the withdrawal is checkable."
  },
